From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] relocate BZI6 resolver to matching SYSTEM dependency namespace

# Reason: patch0210 device logcat:10639 cannot resolve fmt::v12::vformat from BZI6 resolver in S22 Tethering namespace. SYSTEM libbase and its BZI6 dependency group supply the required API; replacing S22 libbase would break its older consumers.
# Affected: existing diagnostic APEX builder/lock, postboot staging helper, finalizer metadata and real ext4 image gate. Selected mode removes the resolver/TLS transplant from APEX, stages the same pinned resolver in SYSTEM, and moves exactly one linker.config.pb declaration from requireLibs(field4) to provideLibs(field3). Normal profile/kernel/vendor/radio unchanged.
# Verify: matched inner/outer manifests, exact payload allowlist, AVB/v3/alignment and two identical selected APEX outputs; fourteen exact SYSTEM provider pins plus statsd; positive and mutated-provider work fixtures; namespace-aware static audit rejects old fmt mismatch and accepts SYSTEM closure. Real device boot is still a separate gate.
# Rollback: restore backed-up APEX and linker.config.pb, remove the added SYSTEM resolver; reverse0211 for source. Preserve protected raw hashes, no BOOT/radio writes.

